# RENDERED OUTPUT, at any depth. `experiments/*/renders/` missed
# `experiments/007-frameworks/three-vanilla/renders/` by one path segment, and
# the untracked tree held 284 MB of video and synthesised speech under paths
# like that. Every one of them is regenerable by a command in the sibling
# README, and where a render is EVIDENCE the writeup cites it by path and says
# how to remake it — which is the durable record, not the bytes. Anything that
# genuinely must ship is force-added.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mp3
*.wav
.*.mp4.parts/
experiments/**/audio/
experiments/**/deck/
experiments/**/deck-*/
experiments/**/out/

# built demo output — regenerate with `npm run demo`
demo/deck/

# synthesised speech — regenerate with `decksmith narrate`. Content-addressed,
# so re-running it after an edit re-speaks only the sentences that moved.
demo/audio/
*.deck

# Scratch that lands HERE rather than in /tmp. `mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), …))`
# resolves against TMPDIR, and agent sessions in this repo run with TMPDIR
# pointing at the working directory.
#
# THIS IS NO LONGER THE FIX, and it was never a good one. `guardTmpdir` in
# src/tmpdir.ts unsets such a TMPDIR, and the CLI, the MCP server, the HTTP
# server and the vitest setup file all call it, so nothing we start writes here
# any more. What is left below is a backstop, and since the accumulation it was
# hiding has been swept it has one job left: covering processes we do not start.
# The sweep was 2026-09-09 — 2,306 directories over eight prefixes, 14MB, plus a
# 34MB `node-compile-cache/` and `tsx-501/`, all of them predating the guard.
#
# THE OLD LIST WAS INCOMPLETE, which is why it is gone. It named ten prefixes and
# missed eight more — `decksmith-harvest-`, `decksmith-drift-`,
# `decksmith-assets-`, `decksmith-transcode-`, `decksmith-prefs-`, `ds-harvest-`,
# and the two FIXED names `decksmith-mcp` and `decksmith-server`, which slipped
# through because `decksmith-server-*/` wants the dash. 2,333 directories had
# accumulated behind that gap when it was counted on 2026-09-08, and `git add -A`
# swept 14 files out of four of them into four separate commits. (The 2,306 above
# is the smaller, later count taken at the sweep itself — two measurements a day
# apart, not a disagreement, which is why both now carry their date.) Two globs cannot go stale the way a list of
# eighteen does, so these are globs; add nothing here without the same property.
#
# ANCHORED, because a glob that cannot go stale can still reach too far. Every
# directory these exist to catch is at the repo root — `mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), …))`
# with `TMPDIR=$PWD` can land nowhere else — but without the leading slash they
# match at any depth: unanchored, `git check-ignore -v` blamed `ds-*/` for both
# `src/ds-helper/x.ts` and `experiments/ds-svg/a.mjs`. `src/emit/morph-runtime.ts`
# already builds to `dist/ds-morph.js`; split that runtime into `src/emit/ds-morph/`
# and the whole directory goes untracked, `git add -A` skips it, and the branch
# builds only on the machine that wrote it.
/decksmith-*/
/ds-*/
# Chrome's own profile directory, and hyperframes' render scratch. Both are
# mkdtemp'd by libraries under whatever TMPDIR the process has — ours is fixed by
# then, but these lines have not been re-measured against a poisoned session.
hf-*/
puppeteer_dev_chrome_profile-*/
# NOT reachable by the guard, for two different reasons, and both measured
# rather than assumed. `node-compile-cache/` is ours but arrives TOO EARLY:
# node enables its compile cache at process startup, before any setup file or
# entry point can run, so it still appears in the tree on a poisoned
# `npx vitest run` with the guard working perfectly. `tsx-*/` is not ours at all
# — there is no tsx in this repo — and belongs to whatever launched the session.
node-compile-cache/
tsx-*/
# No producer found in src/, scripts/, the justfile or CI, and no such directory
# on disk. Predates the rest of this block; left because nobody can name what
# made it.
.scratch/

# `.planning/` itself IS tracked — the experiment records and design notes in it
# are the durable history. These two are not:
#
#   config.json    names a scheduler backend and a model id, so it is a statement
#                  about one machine's CLI logins rather than about the project.
#   research/      is autoresearch thread state — hypotheses, generated scripts,
#                  gate positions — regenerated by `gd research` and meaningless
#                  to anyone who did not run that thread.
.planning/config.json
.planning/research/

# One-off probe output from investigations whose durable record is .planning/.
# Kept on disk, out of the history.
.DS_Store
gsap-truth.json
walk-trace.json
grid-16x9.png
grid-full.png
studio.png
pilotB01.png

# Local `just` settings. Read by `set dotenv-load`, so a line here overrides a
# default in the justfile — which is how a machine's own choices (a non-loopback
# DECKSMITH_HOST, a tighter rate limit) stay out of everyone else's checkout.
.env
